Why the split (docs/VISION.md section 28):
everything a customer embeds in their own application or cluster (SDKs, the Grafana
plugin, examples, deployment files) is Apache-2.0 so it can be used without legal
review. The server (services/) is AGPL-3.0 so the platform cannot be resold as a
hosted service without contributing changes back.

Each package directory carries the full licence text. A file is covered by the licence
of the nearest LICENSE file above it in the tree. Third-party dependencies keep their
own licences.

